<title>GERMANY: Sievert-Germany can meet EMU deficit target.</title>
<headline>Sievert-Germany can meet EMU deficit target.</headline>
<dateline>LEIPZIG, Germany 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank council member Olaf Sievert said on Thursday that Germany would meet the deficit criteria laid down in the Maastricht treaty for entry to European economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>Asked whether he believed Germany would meet the three percent deficit to gross domestic product EMU target, Sievert said: &quot;Yes I believe so.&quot;</p>
<p>He also said he was &quot;confident that the three percent can be reached in a manner which fully complies with the rules.&quot;</p>
<p>He declined to comment on what kind of measures he would view as acceptable in order to meet Maastricht criteria.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
